Hmm... ok... an attempt at the letter D.

I really miss the 'drunk' class that existed in nethack++. It
was my personal favorite.
High con, low wis. Poison resistance, Neutral, rubber hose, and
lots and lots of potions to start.
Playing a drunk was a real challenge, and lots of fun.

Conversely, since elves seem to have their own class, then it
seems only fair that dwarves should as well.

High con, str. Low chr, dex.
Begin the game with poison resistance and the ability to id gems (as
per archaeologist).
Get searching at level 3, and magic resistance at level 10.
Lawful.
Starting weapon is a dwarven short sword or an axe
Start the game with one dwarven armour item, with a chance for two.
(dwarven cloak, dwarven-mithril chain, iron shoes, iron helm, dwarvish
 roundshield).
And a pickaxe, and small chance for a oil lamp.

Gods could be based on Tolkein gods (if there were any dwarf gods, not
sure)

Quest nemisis could be an underground monster, a mind flayer more likely.
Quest item could be a magic hammer (or an anvil?). When invoked it
works in much the same way as Drums of Earthquake do now. When wielded
it sheds light (as a lamp) and has a small chance of petrifying anything
it strikes. Also, wielder can move through stone in much the same
way as when polymorphed into a rockmole. Also functions as a pickaxe in
regards to bashing open statues and doors and the like (though you can
not dig with it per se)

Of course, eating dwarf corpses would be a bad idea... as would genociding
them. 

